    "text": "Summary"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000010",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0008-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0008-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0008-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0008-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0008-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0008-l0003"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0008-l0000",
      "p0001-n0008-l0001",
      "p0001-n0008-l0002",
      "p0001-n0008-l0003"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "The Sustainable Development Goals are not just a call to action, but a vision of hope for a better world where all people can thrive, nature can flourish, and societies can prosper in harmony with one another. To achieve sustainable development, it is critical to study relationship between SDGs and select the most effective priority goals."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000011",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0009-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0009-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0009-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0009-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0009-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0009-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0009-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0009-l0004"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0009-l0004",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0009-l0005"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0009-l0000",
      "p0001-n0009-l0001",
      "p0001-n0009-l0002",
      "p0001-n0009-l0003",
      "p0001-n0009-l0004",
      "p0001-n0009-l0005"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "For problem one, A multi-layer network approach was employed to establish a model for an- alyzing the interrelationships and impacts of SDGs, which improved upon the UN\u2019s goal-target- indicator model by obtaining separate networks for each SDG. The final model was derived by computing the Pearson correlation coefficient matrix and network connections. The network mod- els for 10 regions were visualized, revealing that in the WLD region, SDG8 had a positive impact on other SDGs, particularly on SDG4, while SDG17 had a negative impact on 14 SDGs."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000012",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0010-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0010-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0010-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0010-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0010-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0010-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0010-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0010-l0004"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0010-l0000",
      "p0001-n0010-l0001",
      "p0001-n0010-l0002",
      "p0001-n0010-l0003",
      "p0001-n0010-l0004"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "For problem two, we proposed a network-based evaluation algorithm for problem two, which considers feedback mechanisms and time impact to identify achievable goals and assess project effectiveness. Scores for each SDG were visualized for 10 regions, recommending SDG4 in five regions, including WLD and ARB. Achievable goals within 10 years were identified for 9 regions achieving SDG1 and 2 regions achieving SDG17."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000013",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0011-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0011-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0011-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0011-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0011-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0011-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0011-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0011-l0004"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0011-l0004",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0011-l0005"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0011-l0005",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0011-l0006"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0011-l0000",
      "p0001-n0011-l0001",
      "p0001-n0011-l0002",
      "p0001-n0011-l0003",
      "p0001-n0011-l0004",
      "p0001-n0011-l0005",
      "p0001-n0011-l0006"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "For problem three, we proposed a revised plan to analyze the impact of network model changes when implementing a specific SDG, identifying new feasible goals with smaller impact on other SDGs. Using WLD as an example, we modified the network model to account for the one-way impact of achieved SDGs on other SDGs, visualizing and analyzing the results. We used an eval- uation algorithm to determine the optimal priority target, finding that when implementing SDG4 in WLD, the optimal priority shifted to SDG8. We also recommend incorporating technology and digitalization as new development goals, given their positive impact on SDG2, SDG3, SDG7."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000014",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0012-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0012-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0012-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0012-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0012-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0012-l0003"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0012-l0000",
      "p0001-n0012-l0001",
      "p0001-n0012-l0002",
      "p0001-n0012-l0003"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "For problem four, we modified the model to respond to crises/opportunities by introducing a perturbation matrix to represent event impact and exploring its effect on optimal development goals. In the case of WLD/local wars, the optimal goal shifted from SDG1 to SDG17. Analyzing SDG9 under 7 events, we determined that natural disasters had the greatest impact on the UN\u2019s work."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000015",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0004"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0013-l0000",
      "p0001-n0013-l0001",
      "p0001-n0013-l0002",
      "p0001-n0013-l0003",
      "p0001-n0013-l0004"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "For problem five, our hierarchical network modeling approach can be promoted to analyze goal connections and select priority development goals in other fields. It can refine business goals into targets, indicators, and data in companies. We used business goals as an example, established a network model, and determined the optimal priority development goals. Our method is not limited to the SDG field but can also help other organizations and individuals achieve their goals."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000016",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0014-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0014-l0001"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0014-l0000",
      "p0001-n0014-l0001"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "We have concluded that our model has strong robustness, high stability, and good interpretabil- ity. This provides scientific guidance and support for achieving the SDGs."
  },
